# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and machine-local state
#
# Nothing here should ever reach a public repository. The patterns are
# deliberately broad: forcing an explicit `git add -f` for a false positive is
# far cheaper than leaking one private key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.csr
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.ppk
known_hosts
authorized_keys
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.*
*credential*
*secret*
*.kubeconfig

# Lab inventories carry real hostnames, IPs and usernames. Keep templates,
# ignore the filled-in copies.
inventory.ini
hosts.ini
*.local.toml
*.local.conf
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml

# infra/prepare-cloud-init.sh renders user-data from the template with the
# operator's real SSH public key substituted in. Template in, render out.
user-data
!user-data.template

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts
#
# vmlinux.h is a build product: `make bpf` generates it from this machine's
# kernel BTF by default (or from VMLINUX_BTF=<path>), or copies the header
# PREBUILT_VMLINUX_H names -- machine-specific either way, never commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/build/
/target/
/bpf/include/vmlinux.h
*.bpf.o
*.part

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test-bed outputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/research/experiments/runs/
/research/experiments/analysis/
/research/experiments/calibration/
results/
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.log
*.qcow2
*.img
*.iso

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / Rust
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backup copies and patch debris
#
# A stale copy of a file is never a change anyone means to commit, and it is
# indistinguishable from the real file to a reviewer reading a diff. `patch` and
# a failed `git apply` leave `.orig` and `.rej` behind; the `.bak` names are the
# ones this repository's own instructions produce -- docs/usage.md has operators
# back up speeder.toml as `speeder.toml.bak`, and scripts/bootstrap.sh moves an
# existing source tree aside as `<dir>.bak-<timestamp>` rather than deleting it,
# which `*.bak` alone does not match. Nothing here is named this way, so these
# cost nothing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS / agent session state
#
# The CLAUDE.md files (the repository root and bpf/, crates/, config/, docs/,
# infra/, packaging/) are public and committed. What an agent keeps for one
# machine or one person -- .claude/ and CLAUDE.local.md at any level -- is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md
